<div id="recipe-83458-instructions" class="wprm-recipe-instructions-container wprm-recipe-83458-instructions-container wprm-block-text-normal" data-recipe="83458"><h3 class="wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-instructions-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-none" style="">Instructions</h3><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-group"><ul class="wprm-recipe-instructions"><li id="wprm-recipe-83458-step-0-0" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;">Preheat oven to 400&deg;F (204 &deg;C).</div></li><li id="wprm-recipe-83458-step-0-1" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;">Place cherry tomatoes, sliced shallot, minced garlic, and sliced olives in a 9X13 casserole dish.</div><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-media wprm-recipe-instruction-image"><img decoding="async" width="400" height="248" src="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/Olives-and-tomatoes-with-cod-400x248.jpg" class="attachment-medium size-medium" alt="Two images showing how to prepare the tomato and olive mixture." srcset="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/Olives-and-tomatoes-with-cod-400x248.jpg 400w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/Olives-and-tomatoes-with-cod-768x476.jpg 768w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/Olives-and-tomatoes-with-cod-150x93.jpg 150w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/Olives-and-tomatoes-with-cod.jpg 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 400px) 100vw, 400px" data-pin-media="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/Olives-and-tomatoes-with-cod.jpg"></div> </li><li id="wprm-recipe-83458-step-0-2" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;"><span style="display: block;">Drizzle it with 2 tablespoons of olive oil and sprinkle it with salt, pepper, and red pepper flakes, if using. Toss to combine.</span></div></li><li id="wprm-recipe-83458-step-0-3" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;">Transfer to the preheated oven and bake for 15 minutes or until vegetables are softened.</div></li><li id="wprm-recipe-83458-step-0-4" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;">Meanwhile, pat dry cod fillets with paper towels on both sides.</div><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-media wprm-recipe-instruction-image"><img decoding="async" width="400" height="248" src="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/Preparing-cod-to-bake-400x248.jpg" class="attachment-medium size-medium" alt="Person patr drying and seasoning cod filets." srcset="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/Preparing-cod-to-bake-400x248.jpg 400w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/Preparing-cod-to-bake-768x476.jpg 768w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/Preparing-cod-to-bake-150x93.jpg 150w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/Preparing-cod-to-bake.jpg 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 400px) 100vw, 400px" data-pin-media="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/Preparing-cod-to-bake.jpg"></div> </li><li id="wprm-recipe-83458-step-0-5" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;">Drizzle them with 2 tablespoons of olive oil and season with salt and pepper.</div></li><li id="wprm-recipe-83458-step-0-6" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;">Remove the veggies from the oven and carefully nestle the cod fillets and lemon slices in the vegetables.</div></li><li id="wprm-recipe-83458-step-0-7" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;"><span style="display: block;">Bake for 15-17 minutes or until the internal temperature of a cod filet registers 140 &deg;F (60 &deg;C) when a meat thermometer is inserted in the thickest part.</span></div><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-media wprm-recipe-instruction-image"><img decoding="async" width="400" height="248" src="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/Oven-roasted-cod-400x248.jpg" class="attachment-medium size-medium" alt="Mediterranean cod in a casserole dish before and after it is baked." srcset="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/Oven-roasted-cod-400x248.jpg 400w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/Oven-roasted-cod-768x476.jpg 768w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/Oven-roasted-cod-150x93.jpg 150w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/Oven-roasted-cod.jpg 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 400px) 100vw, 400px" data-pin-media="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/Oven-roasted-cod.jpg"></div> </li><li id="wprm-recipe-83458-step-0-8" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;">When ready to serve, transfer a cod fillet to a plate and spoon it with some of the roasted veggies. Sprinkle it with fresh parsley right before serving.</div><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-media wprm-recipe-instruction-image"><img decoding="async" width="400" height="267" src="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/Mediterranean-baked-cod-recipe-400x267.jpg" class="attachment-medium size-medium" alt="Baked cod with tomatoes and olives in a casserole dish." srcset="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/Mediterranean-baked-cod-recipe-400x267.jpg 400w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/Mediterranean-baked-cod-recipe-768x512.jpg 768w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/Mediterranean-baked-cod-recipe-150x100.jpg 150w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/Mediterranean-baked-cod-recipe.jpg 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 400px) 100vw, 400px" data-pin-media="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/Mediterranean-baked-cod-recipe.jpg"></div> </li></ul></div></div>

<div id="recipe-83458-notes" class="wprm-recipe-notes-container wprm-block-text-normal"><h3 class="wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-notes-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-none" style="">Notes</h3><div class="wprm-recipe-notes"><ul>
<li><strong>Yields:</strong> This recipe yields 4 servings of baked cod, with each serving consisting of one fillet and roasted vegetables. The nutritional values below are per serving.</li>
<li><strong>*Don&rsquo;t have cod?&nbsp;</strong>You can use any mild fish like haddock, halibut, or snapper.</li>
<li><strong>Storing &amp; reheating leftovers:&nbsp;</strong>Bring the baked cod to room temperature, place it in an airtight container, and store it in the fridge for up to 2 days.&nbsp; Reheat in a low-heat oven, <span style="font-weight: 400;">300&deg;F (150&deg;C), for 5-7 minutes or until heated thoroughly.</span></li>
</ul></div></div>
